# Attachment upload = encrypt.lu single Blob + Safari large-file chunks

## Default (Chrome / non-Safari, and Safari ≤ 4 MiB)

1. `POST /api/notes/reserve` → note id + upload token
2. One ciphertext Blob (one secretstream FINAL frame)
3. Safari small: XHR `PUT /api/notes/:id/file` + Bearer, then PUT + `?uploadToken=`
4. Chrome: fetch PUT + Bearer, then PUT/POST + query token
5. Untyped Blob body; await warm-up `GET /api/health` on the relay
6. SPA create-note surface: **no COEP/COOP** (keep COEP only on `/llm-ui` + `/test-llm`)
7. Relay CORS: `Allow-Origin` + `Allow-Headers: authorization` + methods — **no** `Allow-Credentials`

## Safari > 4 MiB (WebKit single-PUT cliff)

WebKit aborts multi‑MiB single XHRs (`status: 0`, ~200 ms) even same-site to
`upload-staging.privatenote.ai`. For those files only:

1. ~1 MiB secretstream frames via `encryptFileToSodiumChunks`
2. Headerless `POST /api/notes/:id/file/chunks/:i` with token + sizes in the query string
3. Gate: `usesSingleBlobAttachmentUpload(file.size)` / `SAFARI_SINGLE_BLOB_MAX_BYTES`

## PrivateNote mapping

| encrypt.lu | PrivateNote |
|---|---|
| `relay.encrypt.lu` | `upload.privatenote.ai` / `upload-staging.privatenote.ai` |
| `POST /api/init-upload` | `POST /api/notes/reserve` |
| `PUT /api/upload/:id` | `PUT /api/notes/:id/file` (single Blob) |
| — | `POST /api/notes/:id/file/chunks/:i` (Safari large only) |

Prefer same-site SPA hosts (`privatenote.ai` / `premium.privatenote.ai`); `*.pages.dev` is cross-site to the upload relay.
